{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they saw the Elohim of Israel.</b> They gazed and stared and became liable to death, except that the Holy One, blessed be He, did not want to mix up the joy of the Torah, and waited for Nadav and Avihu until the day of the dedication of the Mishkan, and for the elders until ״וַיְהִי הָעָם כְּמִתְאוֹנְנִים, וַתִּבְעַר בָּם אֵשׁ יהוה וַתֹּאכַל בִּקְצֵה הַמַּחֲנֶה״ (Numbers 11) — among the elders of the camp (Tanchuma)." "<b>Like the work of sapphire brick.</b> It was before Him at the time of the bondage, to remember the distress of Israel, who were enslaved in brick-making (Vayikra Rabbah)." "<b>And like the essence of the heavens for purity.</b> From the time they were redeemed, there was light and joy before Him." "<b>And like the essence.</b> As the Targum renders — a term of appearance." "<b>For purity.</b> A term of clear and lucid."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:19.234889050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}